# Custom Rules for AI Coding Assistant

- **Git Commits & Pushes**: Do not run `git commit` or `git push` commands (or any commands that commit code) unless the user has explicitly requested a commit or push in their current request.
- **Local Variable Naming**: Ensure all local variables are named using `camelCase`.
- **Formatting Standards**: Strictly adhere to formatting in `agents/FORMATTING.md` (4 spaces, LF, Allman braces for types/functions, bracket spacing `( val)`, `< T>`, column alignment).
- **Formatting Standards**: Strictly adhere to formatting in `agents/FORMATTING.md` (4 spaces, LF, Allman braces for types/functions, bracket spacing `( val)`, `< T>`, column alignment, template keywords indented 1 level less than definition).

